  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Show that each of the following numbers is not prime:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$18^3-15^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$18^3-15^3=3\\times819$.\n\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}18^3-15^3&=(18-15)(18^2+18\\times15+15^2)\\\\18^3-15^3&=3(324+270+225)\\\\18^3-15^3&=3\\times819.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$18^3+3^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$18^3+3^3=21\\times279$.\n\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}18^3+3^3&=(18+3)(18^2-18\\times3+3^2)\\\\18^3+3^3&=21(324-54+9)\\\\18^3+3^3&=21\\times279.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$3^{33}+2^{33}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(3^{11}+2^{11})(3^{22}-3^{11}2^{11}+2^{22})$.\n\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3^{33}+2^{33}&=(3^{11})^3+(2^{11})^3\\\\3^{33}+2^{33}&=(3^{11}+2^{11})(3^{22}-3^{11}2^{11}+2^{22}).\\end{align*}$$\nThe first factor exceeds 1. The second is $3^{11}(3^{11}-2^{11})+2^{22}>1$. Thus the number is a product of two integers greater than 1 and is not prime.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$2^{24}+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2^{24}+1=257\\times65281$.\n\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^{24}+1&=(2^8)^3+1^3\\\\2^{24}+1&=(2^8+1)(2^{16}-2^8+1)\\\\2^{24}+1&=257\\times65281.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$4^{15}+27$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4^{15}+27=1027\\times1045513$.\n\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4^{15}+27&=(4^5)^3+3^3\\\\4^{15}+27&=(4^5+3)(4^{10}-4^5\\times3+3^2)\\\\4^{15}+27&=1027\\times1045513.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$5^6-8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5^6-8=23\\times679$.\n\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5^6-8&=(5^2)^3-2^3\\\\5^6-8&=(5^2-2)(5^4+5^2\\times2+2^2)\\\\5^6-8&=23\\times679.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth integer factors exceed 1, so the number is not prime.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
